Revision history for Selecto-Components

Unreleased
    - A canned page shows a multiple text control as a textarea, so a list
      of values can be pasted one per line.
    - Canned pages: a column_layout entry no longer takes a kind; it follows
      from the entry's keys (field, fields, collection, url_prefix,
      row_number), and kind is refused. The former join is a fields entry.
      A collection entry names the association, and the new
      layout_selections builds a detail query's selections from the layout.
    - Canned layout fields and nested fields take a format (a
      Selecto::DateFormat name, such as the new us_date and us_datetime),
      applied in SQL; layout_selections takes the timezone to show them in.
      The display formats are not offered for Explorer grouping.
    - A canned page with one view and no controls shows no filter panel or
      Apply filters button; the results take the full width.
    - Action prerequisite columns (can_<action>, from Selecto's action
      preconditions and transitions) appear in the Explorer as columns and
      Yes/No filters only while the action authorizer shows their action;
      for a hidden action, both are removed from the request's domain.
    - API console 0.5.11: discovers the canonical getResource route (and still
      the customer API's getCustomerResourceVersion), and chooses between POST
      query and GET resource with radio buttons, shown only when the API
      offers resource GET.
    - An authored query-library segment without parameters may filter on
      internal fields, directly or through a view. Segments that take
      parameters remain refused on internal fields.
    - The Explorer grid, its counts and its CSV/TSV/JSON and XLSX exports ask
      Selecto::PostgreSQL for canonical values, which it no longer returns
      by default, so they are unchanged (2.5, not 2.50; ISO timestamps)
      whatever the host's adapter options. Other adapters ignore the option.
    - Exports check their database deadline with defer_rearm, so the server
      timeout is refreshed before each FETCH rather than once per exported
      row (removes a database round trip per row).
    - Faster exports: CSV/TSV/JSON and XLSX exports fetch 100 rows per
      database round trip instead of one (about 7x faster on a 5,000-row,
      20-column PostgreSQL export, more against a remote database). The
      driver buffers at most 100 rows; per-row cell, row and byte checks are
      unchanged. Needs selecto-perl with fetch_size-aware bounded streams;
      older versions keep fetching one row.
    - 0.1.2 security remediation: bound ordinary Explorer/canned rows, nested
      materialization, response bytes and database work; expire stalled export
      delivery leases and require explicit shared-cache namespaces.
    - Admit action input before callbacks, authorize both choice-range bounds,
      distinguish co-domain lookup authorization, and remove executable SQL
      interpolation. SQL diagnostics require deliberate host debug mode.
    - Require Selecto 0.2.2 for the common bounded result execution boundary.
    - Security: protected WebSockets require live authorization; public and
      disabled modes are explicit. Assistant request bodies, shared draft
      storage, query-state expansion and exports have finite enforced budgets.
    - Security: canonical action targets precede host callbacks; empty choice
      membership is validated; private history and saved URL expansion are
      disabled. See README migration and adapter capability requirements.
    - Graph axes that measure counts tick on whole numbers, so small counts
      no longer repeat rounded labels (3, 3, 2, 2, ...).
    - The canned page record dialog uses the theme's panel colour. It fell
      back to white because the shared theme defines no --sc-surface, which
      left the dark palette's light text unreadable.
    - Non-ASCII values in JSON the explorer and canned pages embed in HTML
      (drilldown buttons, carried drilldown and membership filters, data-*
      attributes, permalinks) and in CSV, TSV and JSON exports are UTF-8
      encoded once instead of twice. Submitted JSON and WebSocket messages
      are parsed as the characters Mojolicious already decoded, so a
      membership filter or drilldown with accented text or emoji selects
      exactly that value instead of failing.
    - Nested to-many columns show non-ASCII values. JSON text from drivers
      that return characters (DBD::Pg on a UTF-8 database, DBD::SQLite with
      sqlite_unicode) failed to parse, and the nested table rendered empty.
    - Optional WebMCP tools edit validated query-form drafts without running
      queries. Drafts support revision checks, idempotent apply, manual-edit
      synchronization, one-step undo, and an optional SQLite store.
    - Development tasks resolve the pinned relocatable Perl directly, including
      commands launched through a shell.
    - WebSocket query runs refresh the permalink and export links to match
      the completed query, including assistant-prepared graph drafts.
    - The explorer retargets its row grain: a detail view whose columns all
      come from one to-many association shows that association's rows, a
      summary that reads one to-many association drills down into the rows
      it counted, and a "Rows of" picker lists the domain's declared
      retarget targets and swaps the pickers to the target's fields. The
      rows_of URL parameter carries the grain. Requires Selecto with
      Query->retarget.
    - Security: the record editor no longer signs or verifies snapshots
      with a guessable key. Without a host-set $app->secrets (Mojolicious
      defaults to the app moniker; the editor fell back to
      'selecto-components') the editor answers 500 and refuses saves.
    - Security: the record-editor signature also binds the session's CSRF
      token, the engine tenant, the domain fingerprint and the time the form
      was opened (record_signed_at). A form replayed in another session or
      tenant is refused, and so is one older than the new
      record_editor_max_age option (default 3600 seconds, at most 86400).
    - Security: the explorer refuses (state error) a query-library segment,
      requested or from a view, that reads an internal or redacted field. A
      components.filter_choices filter over an internal field the host did
      not list in filter_fields, and a conditional choice filter over any
      non-public field, accept only their declared choice values with eq,
      ne, in or not_in; the picker no longer offers them a null test.
      Previously a parameterized segment or a range filter probed the hidden
      values row by row.

0.1.0  2026-09-30
    - First CPAN release: Mojolicious plugin providing the Selecto explorer,
      canned search pages, dashboards, record editor, row and selected-row
      actions, and the API Console over htmx 4 WebSockets with GET/POST
      fallbacks.
    - Native-template pages (Selecto::Components::Templates) moved to the
      separate optional Selecto-Components-Templates add-on.
    - Licensed under the Artistic License 2.0.
    - Strict Content-Security-Policy clean: no inline styles; heat and rollup
      cells use shared theme classes and host theme colours load from a
      validated same-origin stylesheet (Selecto::Components::ThemeStylesheet).
